WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.794
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:10.829 --> 00:00:11.837
Sammy.

00:00:12.296 --> 00:00:14.173
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can.

00:00:14.208 --> 00:00:15.055
Go!

00:00:17.885 --> 00:00:20.095
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:22.406
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:25.476 --> 00:00:26.650
This is dad's book.

00:00:26.685 --> 00:00:28.771
I think dad wants us to
pick up where he left off.

00:00:28.806 --> 00:00:30.814
You know, saving people. Hunting things.

00:00:30.849 --> 00:00:32.399
The family business.

00:00:32.566 --> 00:00:33.866
I got to find dad.

00:00:33.901 --> 00:00:36.153
That's the only thing I can think about.

00:02:04.341 --> 00:02:05.724
I know you're just doing your job

00:02:05.759 --> 00:02:08.073
But the police have
been here a week already.

00:02:08.108 --> 00:02:10.353
I don't see why we have
to go through this again.

00:02:10.388 --> 00:02:13.350
The more he tells the story
the more he believes it's true.

00:02:13.385 --> 00:02:14.809
Mrs. McKay.

00:02:16.597 --> 00:02:18.403
We know you spoke with
the local authorities.

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:22.337
But this seems like a matter
for the State Police. So...

00:02:22.372 --> 00:02:25.003
Don't worry about how
crazy it sounds Evan.

00:02:25.038 --> 00:02:27.130
You just tell us what you saw.

00:02:27.165 --> 00:02:29.295
I was up late...

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:31.391
Watching TV.

00:02:31.426 --> 00:02:33.178
When I heard this...

00:02:33.213 --> 00:02:34.978
Weird noise.

00:02:35.013 --> 00:02:38.078
What did it sound like?

00:02:38.113 --> 00:02:41.144
It sounded like a monster.

00:02:42.604 --> 00:02:45.815
Tell the officers what
you were watching on TV.

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:47.525
Um...

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:51.035
Godzilla versus Mothra.

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:53.093
That's my favorite Godzilla movie.

00:02:53.128 --> 00:02:55.081
So much better than the original?

00:02:55.116 --> 00:02:55.900
Totally.

00:02:55.935 --> 00:02:58.298
Yeah, he likes the remake.

00:02:58.488 --> 00:02:59.794
Yuck.

00:02:59.829 --> 00:03:01.513
That's what I mean.

00:03:03.917 --> 00:03:05.133
Evan?

00:03:05.559 --> 00:03:07.879
Did you see what this thing was?

00:03:07.914 --> 00:03:10.253
No, but I saw it grab Mr. Jenkins.

00:03:10.288 --> 00:03:12.592
It pulled him underneath the car.

00:03:12.993 --> 00:03:14.204
Then what?

00:03:16.131 --> 00:03:18.354
It took him away.

00:03:18.389 --> 00:03:21.621
I heard the monster leaving.

00:03:21.656 --> 00:03:24.527
It made this really scary sound.

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:27.398
What did it sound like, Evan?

00:03:27.956 --> 00:03:32.111
Like this whining growl.

00:03:35.016 --> 00:03:36.449
Thanks for your time.

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:43.331
So the local police
have novel out foul play.

00:03:43.966 --> 00:03:45.798
Apparently there were signs of struggle.

00:03:46.572 --> 00:03:48.461
You know, they could be right.
Could just be a kidnapping.

00:03:49.196 --> 00:03:51.246
Maybe this isn't our kind of gig.

00:03:51.281 --> 00:03:52.765
Yeah, maybe not.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:54.214
Except for this.

00:03:54.249 --> 00:03:56.425
Dad marked the area, Dean.

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:59.129
Possible hunting grounds
of a phantom attacker.

00:03:59.164 --> 00:04:00.971
Why would he even do that?

00:04:01.006 --> 00:04:05.260
Well, he found a lot of local folk law
about a dog figure that comes out at night,

00:04:05.295 --> 00:04:07.888
Grabs people then vanishes.

00:04:07.923 --> 00:04:09.521
He found this too.

00:04:09.556 --> 00:04:14.687
This county has more missing persons per
capital than anywhere else in the state.

00:04:15.104 --> 00:04:16.078
It is weird.

00:04:16.563 --> 00:04:17.450
Yeah.

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:20.491
Don't phantom attackers usually
snatch people from their beds?

00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:22.044
Jenkins was taken from a parking lot.

00:04:22.079 --> 00:04:23.563
Well, there are all kinds, you know.

00:04:23.564 --> 00:04:27.908
Spring Hill Jack, Spanworm Gases,
they take people anywhere, anytime.

00:04:27.943 --> 00:04:30.077
Look, Dean. I don't know if
this is our kind of gig either...

00:04:30.112 --> 00:04:33.163
Yeah, you're right. We should
ask around more tomorrow.

00:04:33.198 --> 00:04:34.623
Right.

00:04:35.666 --> 00:04:38.043
I saw a motel about five miles back.

00:04:38.078 --> 00:04:39.593
Whoa, whoa, easy.

00:04:39.628 --> 00:04:41.547
Let's have another round?

00:04:41.713 --> 00:04:43.138
We should get an early start.

00:04:43.173 --> 00:04:46.343
Now, you really know how to
have fun, don't you Grandma?

00:04:48.261 --> 00:04:49.375
You're right.

00:04:50.463 --> 00:04:52.444
I'll meet you outside.
I'm gonna take a leak.

00:06:40.222 --> 00:06:41.605
Hey, hey.

00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:44.519
Have you guys been outside? Around
here like the last hour or so?

00:06:45.936 --> 00:06:47.104
Sam?

00:06:49.815 --> 00:06:51.176
Sammy!

00:07:10.503 --> 00:07:12.088
Sam...

00:07:23.766 --> 00:07:26.811
So, what can we do for
you Officer Washington?

00:07:26.846 --> 00:07:28.736
I'm working a missing persons.

00:07:28.771 --> 00:07:31.899
I didn't know the Jenkins case was
being covered by the State Police?

00:07:31.934 --> 00:07:34.318
Uh, no, no. It's someone else.

00:07:34.353 --> 00:07:36.035
Actually it's my cousin.

00:07:36.070 --> 00:07:39.198
We were having a few laughs at
this bar down by the highway.

00:07:39.233 --> 00:07:41.081
And I haven't seen him since.

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:44.060
Did your cousin have a drinking problem?

00:07:44.095 --> 00:07:46.661
Sam? Two beers and he's doing Karaoke.

00:07:46.903 --> 00:07:49.833
No, he wasn't drunk. He was taken.

00:07:51.794 --> 00:07:53.712
All right. What's his name?

00:07:53.747 --> 00:07:55.214
Winchester.

00:07:56.465 --> 00:07:57.966
Sam Winchester.

00:07:58.508 --> 00:07:59.694
Like the riffle?

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:01.387
Like the riffle.

00:08:01.512 --> 00:08:03.103
Winchester, Sam

00:08:08.018 --> 00:08:09.985
Samuel Winchester.

00:08:10.020 --> 00:08:15.651
So you know that his brother
Dean Winchester died in St. Louis.

00:08:15.818 --> 00:08:18.654
And it was excepted a murder.

00:08:19.251 --> 00:08:20.906
Yeah, Dean.

00:08:21.508 --> 00:08:23.701
Kind of the black sheep of the family.

00:08:23.736 --> 00:08:25.232
Handsome though.

00:08:30.259 --> 00:08:32.042
Well, he's not showing up
at any current field reports.

00:08:32.077 --> 00:08:34.155
I already have a lead.

00:08:34.816 --> 00:08:37.047
I saw surveillance
camera above the highway.

00:08:37.082 --> 00:08:38.582
County traffic cam.

00:08:38.617 --> 00:08:39.774
Right, yeah.

00:08:39.809 --> 00:08:41.427
I'm thinking the camera
picked up whatever took him.

00:08:41.462 --> 00:08:43.470
Oh, whoever.

00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:46.890
Well, I have access to
the traffic cam footage

00:08:46.925 --> 00:08:49.723
Down at the county
works department, but...

00:08:49.758 --> 00:08:52.521
Well... Let me tell
you this the right way.

00:08:52.556 --> 00:08:56.442
Won't you fill out...

00:08:57.178 --> 00:08:58.993
A missing persons report.

00:09:02.102 --> 00:09:03.949
And sit tight over here.

00:09:04.805 --> 00:09:06.243
Officer, look uh...

00:09:07.432 --> 00:09:08.516
He's family.

00:09:09.156 --> 00:09:10.170
And I kind of...

00:09:11.134 --> 00:09:12.131
Look out for the kid.

00:09:13.074 --> 00:09:14.439
You got to let me go with you.

00:09:14.944 --> 00:09:16.411
I'm sorry, I can't do that.

00:09:18.221 --> 00:09:19.729
Well, tell me something.

00:09:19.764 --> 00:09:22.642
Your county has a fair
share of missing persons.

00:09:22.677 --> 00:09:25.478
Any of them come back?

00:09:26.187 --> 00:09:29.816
Sam's my responsibility.
And he's coming back.

00:09:29.851 --> 00:09:32.151
I'm bringing him back.

00:10:18.556 --> 00:10:19.689
Greg.

00:10:19.724 --> 00:10:21.559
I think we've got something.

00:10:22.768 --> 00:10:24.979
These traffic cam take an
image every three seconds.

00:10:25.014 --> 00:10:27.279
It's part of the amber alert program.

00:10:27.314 --> 00:10:31.902
These images were all taken around
the time your cousin Sam disappeared.

00:10:32.653 --> 00:10:34.084
This really isn't what I'm looking for.

00:10:34.119 --> 00:10:34.812
Just wait, wait.

00:10:34.857 --> 00:10:36.038
Next one.

00:10:36.073 --> 00:10:39.201
This one was taken right
after Sam left the bar.

00:10:39.236 --> 00:10:41.996
Look at the back in at that thing.

00:10:42.663 --> 00:10:45.207
Now, look at the plates.

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:49.427
The plates look new. Probably stolen.

00:10:49.462 --> 00:10:53.716
So, whoever's driving that
rust bucket must be involved.

00:11:00.473 --> 00:11:01.673
Do you hear that engine?

00:11:01.708 --> 00:11:02.939
Yeah.

00:11:03.893 --> 00:11:06.812
Kind of a whining growl, isn't it?

00:11:07.229 --> 00:11:09.148
Sure.

00:11:11.525 --> 00:11:13.486
I'll be damned.

00:11:28.417 --> 00:11:30.294
You're alive?

00:11:31.128 --> 00:11:32.428
Hey, you okay?

00:11:32.463 --> 00:11:35.424
Does it look like I'm doing okay?

00:11:36.552 --> 00:11:37.655
Where are we?

00:11:37.690 --> 00:11:39.220
I don't know.

00:11:39.903 --> 00:11:41.103
Country, I think.

00:11:41.757 --> 00:11:43.328
Smells like the country.

00:11:44.002 --> 00:11:45.518
You're Jenkins, aren't you?

00:11:46.054 --> 00:11:46.977
Yeah.

00:11:48.835 --> 00:11:50.272
Wow, I was looking for you.

00:11:50.603 --> 00:11:51.400
Oh, yeah?

00:11:51.435 --> 00:11:52.197
Yeah.

00:11:52.232 --> 00:11:55.826
Well, no offense. But
this is a piss poor rescue.

00:11:55.861 --> 00:11:59.406
Well, my brother's out there right
now too. He's looking for us. So...

00:11:59.441 --> 00:12:01.551
So, he's not gonna find us.

00:12:01.586 --> 00:12:03.626
We're in the middle of nowhere.

00:12:03.661 --> 00:12:06.580
Waiting for them to come back
and do God knows what to us.

00:12:06.615 --> 00:12:08.339
What are they?

00:12:09.061 --> 00:12:09.775
Have you seen them?

00:12:10.476 --> 00:12:10.702
What are you talking about?

00:12:10.703 --> 00:12:12.586
Whatever grabbed us,
what did they look like?

00:12:12.621 --> 00:12:14.338
See for yourself.

00:12:33.482 --> 00:12:34.615
Leave me alone.

00:12:35.384 --> 00:12:37.278
Don't touch me. Leave me alone!

00:12:54.619 --> 00:12:56.788
I'll be damned.

00:12:59.624 --> 00:13:01.216
They're just people.

00:13:01.251 --> 00:13:04.504
Yeah, what did you expect?

00:13:04.921 --> 00:13:06.568
How often do they feed you?

00:13:06.603 --> 00:13:07.691
Once a day.

00:13:08.008 --> 00:13:11.511
They use that thing over
there to open the cage.

00:13:12.220 --> 00:13:14.055
And that's the only time you see them?

00:13:14.090 --> 00:13:16.474
So far. But I'm waiting.

00:13:16.509 --> 00:13:18.410
Waiting for what?

00:13:18.445 --> 00:13:20.276
Their baiting time, man.

00:13:20.311 --> 00:13:22.536
I think that's the least
of your worries right now.

00:13:22.571 --> 00:13:23.303
Oh, yeah?

00:13:23.338 --> 00:13:23.738
Yeah.

00:13:23.773 --> 00:13:25.028
What do you they want then?

00:13:25.685 --> 00:13:27.575
Depends on who they are.

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:30.613
They're bunch of psycho
hill-Billy red neck if you ask me.

00:13:30.648 --> 00:13:33.366
Looking for love in
all the wrong places.

00:13:47.752 --> 00:13:49.973
Okay, the next traffic cam

00:13:50.008 --> 00:13:53.595
Is fifty miles from here and your
pickup didn't pass that one. So...

00:13:53.630 --> 00:13:55.572
So, it must have pulled up somewhere.

00:13:56.016 --> 00:13:57.480
I don't see any other roads here.

00:13:57.911 --> 00:14:02.020
Well, a lot of these back woods
properties have their own private roads.

00:14:02.523 --> 00:14:03.855
Great.

00:14:16.723 --> 00:14:18.077
So, Gregory.

00:14:18.593 --> 00:14:19.085
Yeah.

00:14:19.887 --> 00:14:21.128
I ran your badge number.

00:14:21.163 --> 00:14:23.860
It's routine when working
A case with State Police

00:14:23.895 --> 00:14:25.752
For county purposes when we have you.

00:14:26.445 --> 00:14:29.589
And they just got back to me...

00:14:33.213 --> 00:14:35.386
Says here your badge was stolen.

00:14:36.172 --> 00:14:39.377
And there's a picture of you.

00:14:44.080 --> 00:14:45.425
I lost some weight.

00:14:45.460 --> 00:14:47.807
And I got that Michael
Jackson skin disease...

00:14:47.842 --> 00:14:48.585
Okay.

00:14:48.620 --> 00:14:50.100
Would you step out of the car please?

00:14:50.135 --> 00:14:51.003
Look, look, look.

00:14:53.053 --> 00:14:55.222
If you want to arrest me that's fine.

00:14:55.257 --> 00:14:57.433
I'll cooperate. I swear.

00:14:57.468 --> 00:14:59.608
But first please...

00:14:59.643 --> 00:15:00.635
Let me find Sam.

00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:02.192
I don't even know who you are.

00:15:02.514 --> 00:15:04.696
Or if this Sam person is missing.

00:15:04.731 --> 00:15:07.067
Look into my eyes and tell
me if I'm lying about this.

00:15:07.102 --> 00:15:10.561
Identity theft. You're
impersonating an officer.

00:15:11.607 --> 00:15:13.273
Here's the thing. When...

00:15:13.564 --> 00:15:15.416
When we were young...

00:15:15.451 --> 00:15:18.458
I pretty much pulled him from a fire.

00:15:19.496 --> 00:15:22.635
And ever since then I
felt responsible for him.

00:15:23.097 --> 00:15:26.628
You know, like it's my
job to keep him safe.

00:15:28.672 --> 00:15:32.968
I'm just afraid if we
don't find him fast.

00:15:33.927 --> 00:15:35.888
Please...

00:15:36.346 --> 00:15:39.308
He's my family.

00:15:40.100 --> 00:15:42.234
I'm sorry.

00:15:42.269 --> 00:15:44.730
You've given me no choice.

00:15:44.765 --> 00:15:47.191
I have to take you in.

00:16:00.897 --> 00:16:03.838
After we find Sam Winchester.

00:16:06.543 --> 00:16:08.072
What's your name again?

00:16:08.107 --> 00:16:09.382
It's Sam.

00:16:09.946 --> 00:16:13.325
Why won't you give it up
Sammy. There's no way out.

00:16:13.360 --> 00:16:14.951
Don't...

00:16:15.535 --> 00:16:17.078
Call me...

00:16:17.113 --> 00:16:18.621
Sammy.

00:16:21.082 --> 00:16:23.460
What is it?

00:16:27.464 --> 00:16:28.805
It's a bracket.

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:32.594
Well, thank God a bracket.
Now we got them, huh?

00:16:34.888 --> 00:16:37.474
Must have been a short.

00:16:40.226 --> 00:16:43.521
Maybe you knocked something loose.

00:16:46.399 --> 00:16:48.117
I think you should get
back in there Jenkins.

00:16:48.152 --> 00:16:48.711
What?

00:16:49.187 --> 00:16:50.869
This isn't right.

00:16:50.904 --> 00:16:52.885
Do you want to get out of here?

00:16:52.920 --> 00:16:54.831
Yeah, but that was too easy.

00:16:54.866 --> 00:16:57.077
Look, I'm gonna get out of
here. I'm gonna send help. Okay?

00:16:57.112 --> 00:16:57.934
Okay. Don't worry.

00:16:57.969 --> 00:16:58.629
No.

00:16:58.664 --> 00:17:01.456
I'm serious, Jenkins.
This might be a trap.

00:17:01.491 --> 00:17:03.416
Bye, Sammy.

00:17:03.708 --> 00:17:05.627
Jenkins!

00:17:45.416 --> 00:17:47.376
Thank you.

00:19:20.444 --> 00:19:22.195
Okay, officer.

00:19:22.446 --> 00:19:24.021
Look I'm gonna press my luck.

00:19:24.056 --> 00:19:25.976
Your luck is so pressed.

00:19:26.276 --> 00:19:27.909
Right.

00:19:28.201 --> 00:19:30.078
I was wondering...

00:19:30.328 --> 00:19:32.726
Why are you helping me out anyway?

00:19:32.761 --> 00:19:35.125
Why don't you just lock me up?

00:19:36.042 --> 00:19:39.379
My brother Riley
disappeared three years ago.

00:19:39.414 --> 00:19:41.763
A lot like Sam.

00:19:41.798 --> 00:19:43.675
We searched for him but...

00:19:43.710 --> 00:19:45.927
Nothing.

00:19:46.595 --> 00:19:49.514
I know what it's like to
feel responsible for someone.

00:19:49.549 --> 00:19:51.850
And for them...

00:19:54.436 --> 00:19:57.006
Come on, let's keep at it.

00:20:00.567 --> 00:20:02.792
Wait, wait. Pull over here. Pull over.

00:20:14.551 --> 00:20:16.718
It's the first turn
off I've seen so far.

00:20:17.792 --> 00:20:19.544
You stay here, I'll check it out.

00:20:19.579 --> 00:20:20.680
No way.

00:20:20.715 --> 00:20:21.781
Hey...

00:20:22.464 --> 00:20:24.278
You're a civilian.

00:20:24.313 --> 00:20:26.057
And a felon, I think.

00:20:26.092 --> 00:20:28.511
I'm not taking you with me.

00:20:29.037 --> 00:20:30.388
You're not going without me.

00:20:33.624 --> 00:20:35.775
All right. You promise...

00:20:35.810 --> 00:20:39.064
You won't get involved.
You let me handle it.

00:20:39.703 --> 00:20:41.041
Yeah, I promise.

00:20:41.076 --> 00:20:42.984
Shake on it.

00:20:46.911 --> 00:20:48.782
Oh, come on.

00:20:49.532 --> 00:20:51.833
This is ridiculous.

00:20:52.568 --> 00:20:54.612
Katherine, I really think
you're gonna need my help.

00:20:54.647 --> 00:20:57.990
I'll manage. Thank you.

00:21:01.452 --> 00:21:04.372
I got to start carrying paper clips.

00:21:34.985 --> 00:21:36.391
Hello?

00:21:39.615 --> 00:21:41.463
Anybody home?

00:21:56.424 --> 00:21:57.668
Hi.

00:21:59.009 --> 00:22:00.780
How are you?

00:22:06.559 --> 00:22:08.234
Who are you?

00:22:08.269 --> 00:22:12.565
I'm Katherine. I'm a deputy.

00:22:12.600 --> 00:22:14.608
What's your name?

00:22:14.643 --> 00:22:16.242
Missy.

00:22:16.277 --> 00:22:18.737
Missy? That's a pretty name.

00:22:18.772 --> 00:22:21.198
Missy, is your mom home?

00:22:21.233 --> 00:22:23.624
She's dead.

00:22:23.659 --> 00:22:27.496
I'm sorry, what about your dad?

00:22:27.788 --> 00:22:30.082
No?

00:22:31.125 --> 00:22:34.170
Can I come in for a minute?

00:22:34.587 --> 00:22:36.922
I just want you look at a picture.

00:22:36.957 --> 00:22:39.357
Have you seen that guy?

00:22:41.469 --> 00:22:43.825
Look at that picture.

00:22:45.848 --> 00:22:47.356
What?

00:22:47.391 --> 00:22:49.894
That's gonna hurt.

00:22:52.730 --> 00:22:54.363
Missy, sweetheart.

00:22:54.398 --> 00:22:56.901
Go tell your brothers,
I want to see them.

00:22:56.936 --> 00:22:59.487
Yes, daddy.

00:23:16.212 --> 00:23:18.589
Son of a bitch.

00:24:22.226 --> 00:24:24.467
But I've never seen him so angry before.

00:24:24.502 --> 00:24:27.783
Never been followed
by the police before.

00:24:42.830 --> 00:24:45.208
You all right?

00:24:48.252 --> 00:24:51.213
Are you Sam Winchester? Aren't you?

00:24:51.248 --> 00:24:53.003
Yeah.

00:24:53.038 --> 00:24:54.759
You're...

00:24:55.134 --> 00:24:58.471
You're cousin's looking for you.

00:24:59.555 --> 00:25:01.411
Thank God.

00:25:01.446 --> 00:25:03.482
Where is he?

00:25:03.517 --> 00:25:05.519
He uh...

00:25:05.853 --> 00:25:09.065
I cuffed him to my car.

00:25:30.670 --> 00:25:32.421
Sam?

00:25:33.047 --> 00:25:34.382
Are you hurt?

00:25:34.417 --> 00:25:36.133
No.

00:25:36.342 --> 00:25:38.844
Damn, it's good to see you.

00:25:39.595 --> 00:25:42.682
How did you get out of the cuffs?

00:25:42.717 --> 00:25:45.559
I know a trick or two.

00:25:46.560 --> 00:25:48.521
All right.

00:25:48.771 --> 00:25:50.231
Oh.

00:25:50.523 --> 00:25:52.865
These locks they're gonna be a bitch.

00:25:52.900 --> 00:25:56.112
Well, there's some kind of
automatic control. Right there.

00:25:56.347 --> 00:25:58.188
Have you seen them?

00:25:58.223 --> 00:25:59.488
Yeah.

00:25:59.523 --> 00:26:01.734
Dude, they're just people.

00:26:01.769 --> 00:26:03.826
And they jumped you?

00:26:03.861 --> 00:26:07.364
Must be getting a little
rusty there, kiddo.

00:26:07.399 --> 00:26:08.386
What do they want?

00:26:08.421 --> 00:26:09.150
I don't know.

00:26:09.151 --> 00:26:11.010
They let Jenkins go, but...

00:26:11.045 --> 00:26:12.835
That was some sort of trap.

00:26:12.870 --> 00:26:14.947
It doesn't make any sense to me.

00:26:14.982 --> 00:26:16.337
Oh, well that's the point.

00:26:16.372 --> 00:26:17.548
You know with...

00:26:17.583 --> 00:26:21.587
Our usual play mates there's rules,
here's patterns. But with people...

00:26:21.622 --> 00:26:23.429
They're just crazy.

00:26:23.464 --> 00:26:26.008
You see anything else out there?

00:26:26.800 --> 00:26:29.365
He has about a dozen junk cars
out back. Plates from all over.

00:26:29.400 --> 00:26:31.930
So, I'm thinking when they take
someone they take their car too.

00:26:31.965 --> 00:26:36.060
Did you see a black mustang?
Out there about ten years old?

00:26:36.095 --> 00:26:39.605
Yeah, actually I did.

00:26:41.281 --> 00:26:44.284
Your brothers?

00:26:45.494 --> 00:26:47.955
I'm sorry.

00:26:49.247 --> 00:26:52.334
Let's get you guys out of here. Then
we'll take care of those bastards.

00:26:52.369 --> 00:26:54.503
It takes a key, key?

00:26:54.538 --> 00:26:55.844
I don't know.

00:26:55.879 --> 00:26:57.756
All right, I better go find it.

00:26:57.791 --> 00:26:59.424
Hey.

00:26:59.800 --> 00:27:01.718
Be careful.

00:27:01.953 --> 00:27:03.920
Yeah.

00:28:15.325 --> 00:28:17.327
Well, I'll say it again.

00:28:17.362 --> 00:28:19.954
Demons I get.

00:28:20.121 --> 00:28:22.540
People are crazy.

00:29:12.420 --> 00:29:14.026
What the...

00:30:49.986 --> 00:30:52.656
It's okay. I'm not gonna hurt you.

00:30:52.989 --> 00:30:54.699
I know.

00:30:54.908 --> 00:30:56.201
Daddy!

00:30:56.326 --> 00:30:57.661
Daddy!

00:30:57.911 --> 00:30:59.454
Daddy!

00:31:00.080 --> 00:31:01.915
Daddy!

00:31:30.326 --> 00:31:33.413
I'm gonna kick your ass first.

00:31:33.746 --> 00:31:35.665
Then yours.

00:31:47.552 --> 00:31:49.345
Come on.

00:31:49.512 --> 00:31:50.895
Let's hunt.

00:31:50.930 --> 00:31:52.890
Yeah, this one's a fighter.

00:31:52.925 --> 00:31:55.893
Sure be fun to hunt.

00:31:56.561 --> 00:31:58.444
Oh, you got to be kidding me.

00:31:58.479 --> 00:32:00.565
This is what this is about? You...

00:32:00.600 --> 00:32:03.401
You yahoos hunt people?

00:32:04.902 --> 00:32:08.364
You ever killed before?

00:32:08.399 --> 00:32:10.366
What?

00:32:11.659 --> 00:32:14.287
Well, it depends on what you mean.

00:32:14.322 --> 00:32:17.630
I've hunted all my life.

00:32:17.665 --> 00:32:21.377
Just like my father, his before him.

00:32:21.412 --> 00:32:23.504
I've hunted deer...

00:32:23.539 --> 00:32:25.304
And bear...

00:32:25.339 --> 00:32:29.385
I even got a coo-Coo once. Oh boy.

00:32:29.802 --> 00:32:32.597
But the best hunt...

00:32:32.632 --> 00:32:35.099
Is human.

00:32:36.267 --> 00:32:39.068
Oh, there's nothing like it.

00:32:39.103 --> 00:32:43.573
Holding their life in your hands.

00:32:43.608 --> 00:32:48.529
Seeing the fear in their
eyes just before they go dark.

00:32:48.564 --> 00:32:52.450
Makes you feel powerful alive.

00:32:52.685 --> 00:32:55.403
You're a sick puppy.

00:32:56.070 --> 00:32:58.246
We give them a weapon.

00:32:58.281 --> 00:33:01.158
Give him a fighting chance.

00:33:01.393 --> 00:33:03.701
It's kind of like...

00:33:03.736 --> 00:33:06.745
Our tradition passed down

00:33:06.780 --> 00:33:12.001
Father to son, cost
only one or two a year.

00:33:12.036 --> 00:33:17.082
Never enough to bring the lot
down we've never been that sloppy.

00:33:17.117 --> 00:33:19.627
Yeah, well. Don't save yourself short.

00:33:19.662 --> 00:33:22.338
You're plenty of sloppy.

00:33:23.672 --> 00:33:27.635
So what? You're with that pretty cop?

00:33:32.932 --> 00:33:35.935
Are you a cop?

00:33:37.561 --> 00:33:40.112
If I tell you...

00:33:40.147 --> 00:33:44.026
You promise not to make
me into an ash tray?

00:33:48.288 --> 00:33:51.875
Only reason I don't let my
boys take you right here now

00:33:51.910 --> 00:33:55.385
Is that there's
something I need to know.

00:33:55.420 --> 00:33:58.206
Yeah, how about it's not
nice to marry your sister.

00:33:59.077 --> 00:34:04.763
Tell me, any of the cops
go come looking for you?

00:34:04.798 --> 00:34:06.104
Oh, eat me.

00:34:06.139 --> 00:34:09.434
No, no, no. Wait. You actually might.

00:34:11.937 --> 00:34:14.821
You think this is funny?

00:34:14.856 --> 00:34:18.777
You've brought this down on my family.

00:34:20.520 --> 00:34:22.487
All right?

00:34:22.522 --> 00:34:25.546
You want to play games?

00:34:25.581 --> 00:34:28.570
We'll play some games.

00:34:30.864 --> 00:34:35.577
Looks like we're gonna have a
hunt tonight after all, boys.

00:34:35.612 --> 00:34:38.663
And you get to pick the animal.

00:34:38.698 --> 00:34:41.037
The boy or the cop.

00:34:41.072 --> 00:34:43.376
Okay, wait, wait.

00:34:43.960 --> 00:34:46.838
Look, nobody's coming for
me. All right? It's just us.

00:34:46.873 --> 00:34:50.091
You don't choose, I will.

00:34:51.635 --> 00:34:55.055
Oh, you son of a bitch!

00:34:59.726 --> 00:35:02.402
Next time, I'll take an eye.

00:35:02.437 --> 00:35:06.233
All right, all right. The
guy. The guy. Take the guy!

00:35:06.858 --> 00:35:08.617
Lee.

00:35:08.952 --> 00:35:11.412
Go do it.

00:35:11.955 --> 00:35:14.561
Don't let him out though.

00:35:14.596 --> 00:35:17.168
Shoot him in the cage.

00:35:18.294 --> 00:35:20.338
What?

00:35:20.547 --> 00:35:22.323
I thought you said you
were gonna hunt him.

00:35:22.358 --> 00:35:23.589
You're gonna give him a chance!

00:35:23.624 --> 00:35:25.161
Lee!

00:35:25.196 --> 00:35:27.053
When you're done with the boy.

00:35:27.088 --> 00:35:30.014
Shoot the bitch too.

00:35:32.350 --> 00:35:37.814
We're cleaning this mess up before
any more cops come running out here.

00:35:46.614 --> 00:35:48.491
What are you doing?

00:35:56.624 --> 00:35:57.792
Hey!

00:35:59.836 --> 00:36:02.297
You hurt my brother,
I'll kill you. I swear.

00:36:02.332 --> 00:36:04.712
I'll kill you all.

00:36:04.747 --> 00:36:07.093
I will kill you all!

00:36:07.768 --> 00:36:09.645
Lee!

00:36:19.822 --> 00:36:21.490
Damn.

00:36:26.704 --> 00:36:28.372
Lee!

00:36:30.541 --> 00:36:33.210
Jack, you come with me.

00:36:33.245 --> 00:36:34.670
Missy.

00:36:34.879 --> 00:36:37.298
You watch him now.

00:36:46.140 --> 00:36:47.350
Lee?

00:36:47.641 --> 00:36:49.393
Where are you?

00:36:53.439 --> 00:36:54.899
Lee?

00:36:56.976 --> 00:36:59.562
Damn it. Jack, hit the lights.

00:37:00.896 --> 00:37:03.315
They must have pulled the fuses.

00:38:34.857 --> 00:38:36.558
You stupid...

00:38:37.559 --> 00:38:38.810
Hey!

00:39:14.762 --> 00:39:16.723
I'll watch this one. You go ahead.

00:39:21.402 --> 00:39:23.988
Go ahead.

00:39:34.457 --> 00:39:36.883
You hurt my family.

00:39:36.918 --> 00:39:39.441
I'm gonna bleed you bitch.

00:39:39.476 --> 00:39:41.965
You killed my brother.

00:39:42.000 --> 00:39:44.342
Your brother?

00:39:45.552 --> 00:39:47.435
Now I see.

00:39:47.470 --> 00:39:50.056
Just tell me why.

00:39:51.567 --> 00:39:54.310
Because it's fun.

00:40:17.174 --> 00:40:17.988
Where's the girl?

00:40:18.023 --> 00:40:19.391
I locked her in the closet.

00:40:19.426 --> 00:40:21.553
What about the dad?

00:40:23.180 --> 00:40:26.809
Shot. Trying to escape.

00:40:37.444 --> 00:40:40.697
I think the car's at the police station.

00:40:40.864 --> 00:40:44.159
Backup units on route to your location.

00:40:46.745 --> 00:40:48.580
So...

00:40:48.914 --> 00:40:52.209
State Police and the FBI are
gonna be here within the hour.

00:40:52.244 --> 00:40:55.128
They're gonna want to talk to you.

00:40:55.629 --> 00:40:59.925
I suggest that you're
both long gone by then.

00:41:00.092 --> 00:41:01.927
Thanks.

00:41:04.137 --> 00:41:05.910
Hey, listen. I don't
mean to press our luck.

00:41:05.945 --> 00:41:07.683
But we're kind of in
the middle of nowhere.

00:41:07.718 --> 00:41:10.060
You think we could catch a ride?

00:41:10.095 --> 00:41:12.354
Start walking.

00:41:13.438 --> 00:41:15.857
Duck if you see a SWAT car.

00:41:15.892 --> 00:41:18.277
Sounds great to me. Thanks.

00:41:18.986 --> 00:41:20.904
Listen...

00:41:22.639 --> 00:41:25.433
I'm sorry about your brother.

00:41:25.892 --> 00:41:27.894
Thank you.

00:41:29.229 --> 00:41:30.779
It was really hard not
knowing what happened to him.

00:41:30.814 --> 00:41:36.319
I thought it would be easier
once I knew the truth. But...

00:41:37.445 --> 00:41:39.864
It isn't really.

00:41:44.703 --> 00:41:47.330
Anyway you should go.

00:42:00.593 --> 00:42:03.096
Don't ever do that again.

00:42:03.131 --> 00:42:04.270
Do what?

00:42:04.305 --> 00:42:06.266
Go missing like that.

00:42:07.684 --> 00:42:09.978
You were worried about me.

00:42:10.729 --> 00:42:14.399
I'm saying, you vanish like that
again I'm not looking for you.

00:42:14.691 --> 00:42:15.711
Sure you will.

00:42:15.746 --> 00:42:16.468
I'm not.

00:42:17.318 --> 00:42:19.577
So you got saddled on by
a 13 year old girl, huh?

00:42:19.612 --> 00:42:20.598
Oh, shut up!

00:42:20.633 --> 00:42:22.570
Just saying getting rusty there, kiddo.

00:42:23.116 --> 00:42:24.784
Shut up!



